  <h1>Paint The Sky With Stars (1997)</h1>
                
                <a class="new-amazon-album-link" href="https://amzn.to/49vcwPf" rel="nofollow sponsored noopener" target="_blank">
                    <Image  src={ptsws} alt="Paint The Sky With Stars (1997)"  width="300" height="300" /></a>
                
                <h2>Album Overview</h2>

                <p>Released on <strong>3 November 1997</strong> in Europe by <strong>WEA</strong> and <strong>11 November 1997</strong> in the United States by <strong>Reprise Records</strong>, <strong><em>Paint the Sky with Stars: The Best of Enya</em></strong> is the definitive first greatest hits collection by Irish singer and composer <strong>Enya</strong>.</p>
                
                <p>Spanning 16 tracks across a total length of <strong>57:46</strong>, the album takes listeners on a sweeping retrospective through a decade of celebrated recordings made between <strong>1986 and 1997</strong>.</p>

                <p><a href="https://amzn.to/49vcwPf" rel="nofollow sponsored noopener" target="_blank">Stream or download Enya songs</a></p>

                <h3>Curated Career Retrospective</h3>

                <p>The collection features 14 carefully selected works from her self-titled debut <a href="/enya-album/"><em>Enya</em></a> (1987), her global breakthrough <a href="/enya-album/"><em>Watermark</em></a> (1988), the multi-platinum <a href="/enya-album/"><em>Shepherd Moons</em></a> (1991), and <a href="/the-memory-of-trees/"><em>The Memory of Trees</em></a> (1995).</p>

                <p><strong>Enya</strong> described assembling the compilation as being "like a musical diary," with each melody evoking vivid personal memories and distinct creative milestones.</p>

                <h3>New Track Additions</h3>

                <p>Intertwined within this retrospective are two newly written compositions: the title track <a href="#Paint_the_Sky_with_Stars">"Paint the Sky with Stars"</a> and the vibrant single <a href="#Only_If...">"Only If..."</a>.</p>

                <p>The lead single <a href="#Only_If...">"Only If..."</a> was released on <strong>10 November 1997</strong> to accompany the worldwide release of the album.</p>

                <h2>Critical Reception & Commercial Success</h2>

                <p><strong><em>Paint the Sky with Stars</em></strong> received universal acclaim from music critics, with <strong>Stephen Thomas Erlewine</strong> of <strong>AllMusic</strong> awarding it a perfect <strong>5 out of 5 stars</strong> rating.</p>

                <p>The album swiftly ascended global music charts, reaching <strong>number 4</strong> on the <strong>UK Albums Chart</strong> and securing the <strong>number 30</strong> position on the <strong>Billboard 200</strong> in the United States.</p>

                <h3>Global Sales & Accolades</h3>

                <ul>
                    <li><strong>United States</strong>: Certified <strong>4× Platinum</strong> by the <strong>RIAA</strong> for shipping over <strong>4,000,000 copies</strong> by 2005.</li>
                    <li><strong>Japan</strong>: First non-Japanese album under the Warner label to receive a <strong>Japan Gold Disc Award</strong> in the Grand Prix Album category for selling over <strong>1,000,000 copies</strong>.</li>
                    <li><strong>Worldwide</strong>: Reached total global sales exceeding <strong>12,000,000 copies</strong>.</li>
                    <li><strong>Europe</strong>: Awarded a <strong>3× Platinum</strong> certification by the <strong>IFPI</strong> for selling over 3 million units across the continent.</li>
                </ul>

                <p>To promote the release, <strong>Enya</strong> embarked on an extensive media circuit featuring television broadcasts and international interviews.</p>
            
                <p>Jump to <a href="#lyrics">lyrics</a>, <a href="#videos">videos list</a>, <a href="#linernotes">liner notes</a> and <a href="#credits">credits</a>.</p>
                
